//! The prose of `ClientHost::set_block_extra_models` (#2763), kept out of `notes.rs`.
pub trait Notes {
    #[notes = r#"## Block extra models

`ClientHost::set_block_extra_models(pos, models)`: the standalone models (`RenderAssets::model`) a client mod draws as part of the block at `pos`, chosen at run time, as NeoForge's `ModelData` lets a block's model choose parts without a block state for each (a cable's per-side channel counts). The chunk mesher draws them after the block's own models, in its light and tints, each quad in its own render layer, and culls faces with a cull direction by the neighbour as it culls the block's. A list replaces the last (empty clears it, at most `BLOCK_EXTRA_MODELS_MAX`, 64) and the section is meshed again when it changes. Client-only and kept in the client's column (`Chunk::extra_models`), so the workers read it and call no mod code; cleared when the block state changes, the column unloads or the player's level changes; no block entity needed. A section's extra models are held to its quad and byte limits after the blocks' own geometry; past them, the rest (block order, then list order) are not drawn. World-only: resolve new handles in `client_resources_reloaded` and set the lists again from the next World-phase callback (`client_tick_pre`). Refusals are named (`BlockExtraModelsError`: `NotLoaded`, `TooMany`, `Model`, and `Unavailable` outside the World phase, on both targets). Native and wasm mods make the same call."#]
    fn block_extra_models();
}
